# Design-time agents

Definitions live in `.claude/agents/` (read by Claude Code and Cursor); the workflow is the
`init-c-dags` skill in `.claude/skills/init-c-dags/`. Agents prepare evidence and drafts; humans sign.

| Phase | Agent | Writes | Closes with |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 Discovery | `source-scout` | `discovery.md` (probes via `make probe`) | `make advance` |
| 2 Assessment | `source-assessor` | `assessment.md` | **H1** signed by a human |
| 3 Blueprint | `silver-designer` | `contract*.yml`, `blueprint.yml` | `make review` passes |
| 3 Review | `arch-reviewer` | `review.md` notes only | **H2** signed by a human |

Commands: `make status|advance|review|probe ID=<id>`. `make sign` is **human only** and refuses
agent shells and non-interactive terminals. Never edit `state.yml` by hand, never approve a gate.
